      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-346064",
      ":question/problem": "Consider the following initial value problem.\n$y^{\u2033} - 9y =-8e^{-t}, y(0) = 2, y^{\u2032}(0) = 2$\n\nSelect the correct options in the reasoning below to find the solution using Laplace transforms.\n\nLet $Y(s) = L{y(t)}$. Taking the Laplace transform of both sides of the equation and solving for $Y$, we have$(2(s - 1))/((s - 3)(s + 1))$ {{field-1}} The partial fraction decomposition of $Y$ is$\\frac{1}{s + 1} + \\frac{1}{s - 3}$ {{field-2}} Therefore, the solution to the initial value problem is$e^{-t} + e^{3t}$ {{field-3}}"
    },
